# Append-only tracker side-file (Parallel-PR §Phase-status collision pattern, #230):
# it only ever grows by appended per-PR entries, so `merge=union` — which keeps
# BOTH sides' lines on a merge/rebase instead of emitting conflict markers — is the
# correct semantic and eliminates the recurring benign "keep both chronological"
# rebase churn when parallel PRs each append an entry. Do NOT add union to
# CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md — those carry substantive edits where interleaving would corrupt.
PHASE_STATUS_INFLIGHT.md merge=union
